  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PGA is an international network of individual, non-partisan  legislators (MPs) from 131 elected parliaments in all regions of the world. The network was founded in 1978. PGA runs projects and programmes which focus on important global issues that no country acting alone can resolve. It generats consensus among lawmakers on treaties, reproductive health, HIV/AIDS, disarmament and int. justice</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Parlamentariker f&#xF6;r Global Action (PGA) &#xE4;r ett internationellt n&#xE4;tverk av parlamentariker, fr&#xE5;n s&#xE5;v&#xE4;l regerande som oppostionspartier, fr&#xE5;n ca 130 l&#xE4;nder v&#xE4;rlden &#xF6;ver. PGA arebtar med fr&#xE5;gor (issue based) inom omr&#xE5;dena s&#xE5;som demokrati och m&#xE4;nskliga r&#xE4;ttigheter, fr&#xE4;mjande av r&#xE4;ttsstaten samt h&#xE4;lsa och befolkningsfr&#xE5;gor.</narrative>
  </description>
